    test(scenario): reconcile fixtures with the one-subject registry (D284)
    
    `dry-run-scenario-composition`:
    - the failed-terminal fixture no longer names the retired
      `finalization-subject-mismatch`; it drives the runtime directly, so what it
      pins is the terminal, not the subject — it now uses the one subject.
    - `CHAIN_BLOCKED_MANIFEST` and its test are DELETED with their premise: the
      committed registry no longer carries a chain subject that is `gone`, and a
      fixture may not invent one into config. The blocked-row-without-a-runtime path
      is still pinned by the finalization case above it (now blocked on the pending
      transaction number), and the chain DISPATCH proof survives in the ready case.
    - the ready chain case runs on `finalization-canary` and captures
      `documentNumber: "4537"`.
    
    `architecture/test-target-registry` — the minimum this unit owns (u1r-c owns the
    T1b manifests and doc 03b's inventory line):
    - every `target.workflow` / `target.kind` / `target.publicInput` access path
      moved to the arm it now lives on
    - the availability pin is re-dated to the 2026-08-28 read-only re-verification
    - the chain-subject table is the one 4537 row
    - "refuses a label owned by another workflow" became "answers both resolvers
      from the one subject's own arm": with one subject declaring both arms, the
      committed registry can no longer exhibit a cross-workflow label, and the
      refusal-BY-NAME path is pinned in the unit file, which can build such a
      subject without committing a false one.
    
    Still RED here, by design, for u1r-c: "registers every T1b manifest label in
    config" and "registers exactly the Kuali documents doc 03b's inventory line
    names".
    
